issues":345,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:15:08Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":10,"created_at":"2026-08-31T16:40:42Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T06:18:18Z","closed_at":"2026-09-17T18:03:51Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nIssue was discovered and is reproducible in v4.7.2.stable.steam [ed1daf0bf]\nIssue is reproducible in v4.7.1.stable.official [a13da4feb]\nIssue is not reproducible in v4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.2.stable (ed1daf0bf) Windows 11 (build 26200) Multi-window, 2 monitors Direct3D 12 (Forward+) dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700F (24 threads) 15.71 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Godot 4.7.2, at least in some cases, the Debugger will freeze in an apparently infinite loop when an out-of-bounds index is used to access an array of integers.\n\nThe debugger shows a long list of stack frames referencing the single line where the access occurs, as if it were calling itself, as seen in this snapshot of the screen.\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1032\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58490a0e-6c45-4a05-a625-ff3558c9cf17\" />\n\nThe debugger continues to run, with new frames added to the stack trace, and, except for the close button in the window's title bar, the application does not recognize user input.\n\nI have included a copy of the project for your examination. (Note that the program is not complete, There are certainly programming errors in the code, but I don't believe they are related to this issue since the program does run in 4.6.3.)\n\n[chess.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31653438/chess.zip)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nImport code provided and run the project.\nNote the apperance of Godot flickering.\nAttempt to pause the debugger.\nAttept to add a breakpoint in the code to stop the debugger.\nAttempt to close Godot by clcking on the X in the upper right of Godot.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nCreate a simple scene with a single Control node, and add the following script to the node:\n\n```gdscript\nextends Control\n\nconst OUT_OF_BOUNDS_INDEX = 10\nvar test_array: Array[int] = []\n\nvar property: int = 0:\n\tget:\n\t\treturn test_array[OUT_OF_BOUNDS_INDEX]\n\nfunc  _ready() -> void:\n\tvar test : int = property\n```","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123042/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123042/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"